    (v("message" |-> v(("attributes" |-> v(("event" |-> v("user_created"), "origin" |-> v("api"), "version" |-> v("1.0"))), "data" |-> v("eyJldmVudCI6ICJ1c3VhcmlvX2NyZWFkbyJ9"), "messageId" |-> v("0"), "publishTime" |-> v(
    "2025-11-19T12:34:56.000Z"), "subscription" |-> v("projects/my-project/subscriptions/my-sub")))) $ v("message" |-> v(("attributes" |-> v(("event" |-> v("user_created"), "origin" |-> v("api"), "version" |-> v("2.0"))), "data" |-> v(
    "eyJldmVudCI6ICJ1c3VhcmlvX2NyZWFkbyJ9"), "messageId" |-> v("1"), "publishTime" |-> v("2025-11-19T12:34:56.000Z"), "subscription" |-> v("projects/my-project/subscriptions/my-sub"))))) >

< subscriber(1) : Subscriber | received : (v("message" |->
    v(("attributes" |-> v(("event" |-> v("user_created"), "origin" |-> v("user"), "version" |-> v("3.0"))), "data" |-> v("eyJldmVudCI6ICJ1c3VhcmlvX2NyZWFkbyJ9"), "messageId" |-> v("2"), "publishTime" |-> v("2025-11-19T12:34:56.000Z"),
    "subscription" |-> v("projects/my-project/subscriptions/my-sub")))) $ v("message" |-> v(("attributes" |-> v(("event" |-> v("user_created"), "origin" |-> v("user"), "version" |-> v("3.0"))), "data" |-> v("eyJldmVudCI6ICJ1c3VhcmlvX2NyZWFkbyJ9"),
    "messageId" |-> v("3"), "publishTime" |-> v("2025-11-19T12:34:56.000Z"), "subscription" |-> v("projects/my-project/subscriptions/my-sub"))))) > < subscriber(2) : Subscriber | received : v("message" |-> v(("attributes" |-> v(("event" |-> v(
    "user_created"), "origin" |-> v("api"), "version" |-> v("1.0"))), "data" |-> v("eyJldmVudCI6ICJ1c3VhcmlvX2NyZWFkbyJ9"), "messageId" |-> v("0"), "publishTime" |-> v("2025-11-19T12:34:56.000Z"), "subscription" |-> v(
    "projects/my-project/subscriptions/my-sub")))) >

rew init .

Publisher

Role: sends messages to the topic.
Key attributes:

* topic_name	Name of the topic it publishes to.	"new-orders"
* message	Message content (JSON or string).	{"order_id": 123, "total": 59.99}
* message_id	Unique ID generated by Pub/Sub.	"msg-7e3a1c"
* attributes	Key-value metadata used for filtering.	{"region": "EU", "channel": "web"}
* ordering_key (optional)	Guarantees ordering of messages with the same key.	"customer_567"
* publish_time	Publication timestamp.	2025-10-10T16:32:00Z
* retry_policy (optional)	Configures automatic retries.	maxRetryDuration=600s

Topic

Role: intermediate channel that receives messages and distributes them to subscriptions.
Key attributes:

Attribute	Description	Example / Detail
* name	Unique identifier of the topic.	"projects/my-project/topics/new-orders"
* message_storage_policy	Regions where messages may be stored.	{"allowedPersistenceRegions": ["europe-west1"]}
* labels	Labels for organization and billing.	{"environment": "production"}
* kms_key_name (optional)	KMS key used to encrypt the topic.	"projects/.../cryptoKeys/..."
* retention_duration	How long unacknowledged messages are retained.

Subscription

Role: connection between a topic and a subscriber.
Key attributes:

Attribute	Description	Example / Detail
* name	Unique name of the subscription.	"subs-orders-inventory"
* topic	Name of the associated topic.	"new-orders"
ack_deadline_seconds	Time to acknowledge (ACK) the message before it is redelivered.	10 – 600 s
push_config (if PUSH)	HTTP endpoint Pub/Sub sends messages to.	"https://myapi.com/webhook"
retry_policy	Delays between delivery retries.	minBackoff=10s, maxBackoff=600s
filter (optional)	Only receives messages that meet the conditions.	"attributes.region='EU'"
dead_letter_policy (optional)	Sends failed messages to another topic.	"dead-letter-topic"
expiration_policy	When to delete inactive subscriptions.	never or 31 days

Subscriber

Role: consumes messages from a subscription (push or pull).
Key attributes:

Attribute	Description	Example / Detail
subscriber_id	Identifier of the consumer.	"svc-payments"
mode	Delivery mode: PUSH or PULL.	"PUSH"
endpoint (if PUSH)	URL where it receives messages.	"https://api.mycompany.com/payments"
ack_mode	Whether acknowledgement is automatic or manual.	"manual"
concurrency	Number of concurrent threads or workers.	5
error_handling	Strategy on failure.	"retry / discard / DLQ"
logging	Logging level.	"info", "debug", etc.
